n't  action censured insofar as it implies a  self-confidence it's already akin to  pride or is an action of sort of  degradation and Marcel says you've  really misunderstood things if you see  it that way why he says the idea of  inert hope is a contradiction in terms  hope is not just waiting around it is  something that underpins and over arches  the action but which inevitably  degenerates or disappears when action  ceases he says I perceive hope as a  prolongation into the unknown of an  activity that is central that is rooted  in one's being  hence it's affinities not with desire  but with one's will hope is a matter of  willing so the will also carries within  itself a refusal to calculate  possibilities or at least a refusal to  be stopped by such a reckoning of  probabilities  so he says couldn't we define hope is an  act of will that applies itself to what  does not depend upon itself you might  say hope is an act of will that connects  the will to something more and beyond  its  with what really matters to the person  it refuses this is something that is  within the realm of our choice it  refuses either to calculate the  possibilities or if it does calculate  the possibilities and probabilities to  be stopped by these calculations and  probabilities to say oh well so I can  happen so therefore I will not hope at  all now we can close by saying should we  hope about everything Marcel doesn't go  into this but I think we can say that we  don't really have the capacity to hope  for every single thing all the time  because hope is an act of will so it  does demand work on our part so we  perhaps need to be thoughtful or careful  about what we're going to devote our  hope to and if we do that if we carry  out this reflection and then carry out  what Marcel thinks of as secondary  reflection that is reflection upon  reflection we might have a better sense  of priority when it comes to the things  that we devote our hope to so very  important concept for Marcel in this  essay concrete approaches to  investigating the ontological mystery  hope is at the center of the ontological  mystery and it is how we connect  ourselves to it  you
 

